   "text": {
    "L1": "Water is found in three forms: liquid, solid ice, and invisible water vapour.",
    "L2": "Liquid water is in seas, rivers, lakes and under the ground. Solid water is ice, snow and glaciers.",
    "L3": "Water vapour is a gas in the air, and we cannot see it.",
    "L4": "Water changes form, but it is never destroyed. A puddle dries when its water evaporates into the air.",
    "L5": "Later, vapour can cool and condense into drops. Water can also freeze into ice and melt again.",
    "L6": "About 97 out of every 100 parts of Earth's water is salty sea water, so most water cannot be drunk.",
    "L7": "Most fresh water is frozen or underground. Less than one part in 100 is in rivers, lakes and reachable ground water.",
    "L8": "Because usable fresh water is shared by everyone, we must not waste or dirty it."
   },
